    "Continue to f_closure_list"

# Summary: This test verifies that:
# 1. GDB can set breakpoints on functions with custom block type parameters
# 2. Closure types are read correctly from DWARF
# 3. Lazy value types work correctly (before and after forcing)
# 4. Reference types and mutable data work
# 5. Exception values are handled correctly
# 6. First-class modules work
# 7. Weak references, hashtables, and buffers work
# 8. Complex nested structures (lazy closures, closure references, closure lists) work
# 9. Program execution through custom block code works correctly
